      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Empty update does not advance the selected-calendar timestamp",
      "description": "`updateManyByCredentialId(this.credential.id, {})` passes an empty update to Prisma. Prisma does not advance an `@updatedAt` field when the update data is empty, so this call does not perform the timestamp update described by its comment. Pass `{ updatedAt: new Date() }` explicitly if this timestamp must track cache refreshes, and add a regression test that verifies it advances.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts:1024"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Delegated calendars cannot display their existing cache",
      "description": "Cache status is looked up exclusively using the credential IDs returned for connected calendars. Delegated connections use the in-memory ID `-1` (`packages/lib/delegationCredential/server.ts`), whereas cache writes use a persisted, positive credential ID through `getCredentialForCalendarCache`.\n\nConsequently, delegated calendars receive `cacheUpdatedAt: null` even when they have cached availability, hiding the cache status and deletion action. Resolve delegated connections to their user-owned persisted cache credentials before querying status, and ensure deletion uses that resolved identity rather than `-1`.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/calendars/connectedCalendars.handler.ts:27-35"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Successful cache deletion can leave stale cache controls visible",
      "description": "The deletion mutation refreshes state only through the optional `onSuccess` callback. Unlike the disconnect mutation, it never invalidates `viewer.calendars.connectedCalendars` itself.\n\nThis fails in the event-type advanced settings: `EventAdvancedTab.tsx` renders `SelectedCalendarsSettingsWebWrapper` without an `onChanged` callback, and that wrapper disables refetching on window focus. After deletion succeeds there, the old timestamp and \u201cDelete cached data\u201d action remain visible. Invalidate the connected-calendars query on successful cache deletion independently of the optional callback, and test this callback-free usage.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "packages/features/apps/components/CredentialActionsDropdown.tsx:41-45"
    }
  ],
